description.narrative:
The Community Land Initiative (iTC) is a Mozambican non-profit organization designed to strengthen the capacity and rights of rural communities to secure the tenure of land and other natural resources, as well as to promote its management and sustainable use with a view to contributing to economic growth and development in rural areas.

The CTC-COOP/iTC-F’s aimed to:

1. Mobilize resources to secure access to land through community land delimitation and demarcation of farmers’ associations land. Use of Social Preparation method, to ensure that the communities in which iTC works are structured; become aware of the laws, their rights and duties; the potential of its resources; the importance of having use plans; including the importance of respect, preserve and enhance the environment, and become key players in their own development.

2. Maintain openness to advise and encourage potential investors to do so in a responsible manner, with respect for the laws and communities, including partnerships with communities that are beneficial and fair to members of these communities, men and women, and the use of land and natural resources, will ensure the improvement of the living conditions of future generations;

3. Ensure liaison with industry partners (government, civil society, private sector, academia) to governance, prioritization of our interventions, dialogue and improvement of methods and policies;

4. Promote the availability of the Community service delivery site in view of the promotion of Local Economic Development (LED).
